Package: cnvstrmliner
Type: Package
Title: Parser and Utilities for managing results from various CNV calling tools
Version: 0.1.185
Authors@R:
    person("Konstantinos", "Mavrommatis",
           email = "konstantinos.mavrommatis@bms.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
URL: https://github.com/kmavrommatis/cnvstrmlineR,
    https://kmavrommatis.github.io/cnvstrmlineR/
BugReports: https://github.com/kmavrommatis/cnvstrmlineR/issues
Description: CNV streamliner.
    The aim of this package is to streamline the analysis of results produced by CNV tools. 
    It introduces the cnvstrml object and parsers for commonly used methods.
    Inputs:
    It has some methods to compare different calls.
    Available support for
    FACETS, PureCN, SCLUST, Sequenza, GATK CopyNumber, ControlFreec (without subclones), Battenberg, CNVkit, SEG (Generic input file for IGV).
    Outputs:
    VCF (v4.2 compliant), SEG, GISTIC2.0 segment files.
    Visualization: 
    This package contains methods to visualize the segments 
    of a genome or of a choromosme 
    or a cohort of samples
    Metrics:
    It also provides metrics for the segmentation result and allows to compare
    CNV calls among samples using standard CNV metrics.
    Using the CNAQC package it provides a PASS/FAIL result for the sample and for
    each segment.
